      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order confirmed; event-level conclusion unresolved\n\nThe available records identify the September manufacturing order ending in **1070**, but access restrictions prevented verification of its cost events.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, Dekoven — **Cooler Plate Pack** |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe timestamp above is reproduced exactly; the source supplies no time zone.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management **26B**, *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* (PDF page **233**, printed page **225**), states that newly created transactions after Pending Close—even when relating to the current or a prior period—will **not be staged or processed** until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nConsequently, the event’s type, creation time, and recorded status are all needed to assess consistency.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe accessible records contain the work order, cost period, and policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. Access to supporting records was denied because my role lacks the required permission. An authorized extract was requested but not received. This does **not** establish that no late event exists.\n\nNo database records were changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_e19faefb6eb4/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains **incomplete—needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
